as an example here. So when Samantha and I were first married and even dating, I wanted

179
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:46,980
to be super relational with her. I went out of my way to make sure she was happy, supported,

180
00:20:46,980 --> 00:20:52,160
felt the love and attention that she deserved. Mostly so she wasn't wise enough to the fact

181
00:20:52,160 --> 00:21:02,280
that she married down. And FYI, her eyesight is terrible. Just saying that. I wanted her to know

182
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:08,660
that she was my top priority. I wanted her to feel loved, appreciated, heard, and validated

183
00:21:08,660 --> 00:21:20,080
as my wife. But eventually came distractions, obligations, children. Life happened with all

184
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:29,100
the busyness of it. But see, God knew all this when he was writing through James. That's

185
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:35,500
the beauty of serving a God that laid down his divinity for humanity. He knows life because

186
00:21:35,500 --> 00:21:41,380
he lived it. If you're married and you enter a covenant with your spouse, if you're Christian,

187
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:47,740
you've entered a covenant with God. So I want to talk about position and condition. My position

188
00:21:47,740 --> 00:21:51,980
as a husband might not change because I don't pay attention to my wife as much or love her the

189
00:21:51,980 --> 00:21:58,240
way I used to or make sure she feels appreciated. See, I'm still her husband. But our condition

190
00:21:58,240 --> 00:22:03,880
on the other hand will definitely change. The condition of our relationship suffers greatly

191
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:10,460
when I don't pay attention to her needs, her happiness, and her feelings. So what's the

192
00:22:10,460 --> 00:22:18,480
fix of this? How do I repair my relationship with God? See, James gives us the answer. This

193
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:27,100
is where I need some involvement. Is it to try to be nicer? No. Is it to try to do better?

194
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:37,400
No. Is it to try to be more faithful? No. Now, if that's what you've been hearing as we've

195
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:42,140
worked through, James, you've missed the point. Either you're doing a really bad job of listening

196
00:22:42,140 --> 00:22:48,320
or we're doing a really bad job of teaching. But see, we're to the hinge here. See, we're

197
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:55,380
at the point where we learn how to turn things around. Relational proximity. Draw near to God

198
00:22:55,380 --> 00:23:00,300
and he will draw near to you. See, James has given us an outline of what it looks like to

199
00:23:00,300 --> 00:23:05,020
be away from God and close to the world. Now let's look at what it looks like to be close

200
00:23:05,020 --> 00:23:10,280
to God and away from the world. The first thing I want to look at in verse six is he gives

201
00:23:10,280 --> 00:23:18,660
grace generously. See, think back to Hosea. He had a small taste of what God has had to deal

202
00:23:18,660 --> 00:23:31,800
with since creation. Since creation, Adam and Eve. But God, unlike us, has continued to be faithful.

203
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:39,380
Continued to love us from the beginning of time to the end of it. God is faithful.

204
00:23:40,660 --> 00:23:47,240
He has nail prints in his hands and his feet that are the evidence of his love. Your life,

205
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:58,720
my life, bears the marks of our unfaithfulness to him. But his life and his body bears the marks of

206
00:23:58,720 --> 00:24:06,180
his faithfulness to you and to me. That's grace. See, grace isn't I've got it all together. See,

207
00:24:06,660 --> 00:24:13,680
grace is, grace isn't I can do whatever I want to with no consequences. Grace is you've made

208
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:20,780
mistakes. They don't define you. Jesus does. For from his faithfulness, we have received grace

209
00:24:20,780 --> 00:24:29,400
upon grace. John 1, 16. But with grace, grace isn't received in a prideful heart. See, James

210
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:35,500
says grace is given when a heart is humbly willing to accept it. So we sang that today. But

211
00:24:35,500 --> 00:24:44,660
how many of us practice that? I heard a sermon one time that talked about how many times you've

212
00:24:44,660 --> 00:24:51,180
sang, I surrender all. You know, the old hymn. How many of us have truly surrendered all?

213
00:24:51,180 --> 00:25:01,380
See, this is the gospel. This is the good news. God's kingdom is at hand. God has returned to his

214
00:25:01,380 --> 00:25:08,220
people. God has taken everything that has due me and ransomed me. He's taken judgment from the only one

215
00:25:08,220 --> 00:25:15,980
capable of delivering it properly. I'm going to say that again because it's for me. He's taken judgment

216
00:25:15,980 --> 00:25:23,720
from the only one capable of delivering it properly. See, Tim Keller puts it like this. The gospel is

217
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:32,080
that we are more sinful and flawed in ourselves than we ever dared believe. Yet, at the very same time,

218
00:25:32,080 --> 00:25:35,740
we are more loved and accepted in Jesus Christ than we ever dared hoped.

219
00:25:39,020 --> 00:25:47,480
And it's because of this that James ends the section like this. God opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble.

220
00:25:47,480 --> 00:25:55,880
So humble yourselves before God. I'm going to say that again because it's for me. Humble yourselves before God.

221
00:25:57,020 --> 00:26:03,100
How is it that we started a conversation about an adulterous affair, and it ends with saying,

222
00:26:03,100 --> 00:26:08,120
humble yourselves to the one whom you've betrayed, and he will exalt you.

223
00:26:08,120 --> 00:26:14,060
We've betrayed God, but God also promises in his faithfulness to exalt us.

224
00:26:14,060 --> 00:26:19,800
Don't shield yourself from this message.

225
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:24,140
Don't withdraw from a message that is heavy-handed about who you are.

226
00:26:26,860 --> 00:26:28,860
Don't defend or deflect it.

227
00:26:28,860 --> 00:26:31,980
Humble yourselves under it.

228
00:26:31,980 --> 00:26:35,460
See, when you humble yourselves under the weight of who you really are,

229
00:26:35,460 --> 00:26:38,040
you begin to see God for who he really is.

230
00:26:38,040 --> 00:26:41,300
This is the moment you can feel God moving in.

231
00:26:41,300 --> 00:26:46,040
This is the moment we not only see ourselves as lawbreakers,

232
00:26:46,040 --> 00:26:47,780
but adulterers.

233
00:26:47,780 --> 00:26:51,820
And we can begin to see how in need of a Savior we truly are.

234
00:26:51,820 --> 00:26:56,660
See, we'll circle back to the easy-come, easy-go type of relationship with God.

235
00:26:56,700 --> 00:27:03,360
Can you think of a more prideful stance than have of the creator of the universe,

236
00:27:03,360 --> 00:27:05,180
the king of kings and the Lord of lords?

