00:27:05,180 --> 00:27:07,020
Preach himself here.

238
00:27:07,020 --> 00:27:10,720
Then I'll give you what you want when I'm good and ready.

239
00:27:12,540 --> 00:27:13,940
Is this the attitude of love?

240
00:27:13,940 --> 00:27:17,020
Is this the attitude of allegiance?

241
00:27:17,020 --> 00:27:21,260
Is this the attitude of the humble?

242
00:27:21,260 --> 00:27:26,060
Stop being too proud to hit your knees.

243
00:27:26,060 --> 00:27:28,160
God's kingdom is upside down.

244
00:27:29,020 --> 00:27:30,340
Humble yourselves before God.

245
00:27:30,340 --> 00:27:32,420
Resist the devil and he will flee from you.

246
00:27:32,420 --> 00:27:38,120
See, Ryan last week talked about the unholy trinity consisting of the world, the flesh, and the devil.

247
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:43,600
See, all three will promise you things that you think will fill the void in your soul.

248
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:45,760
But I can promise you they won't.

249
00:27:45,760 --> 00:27:48,100
You can try them, but I promise they won't.

250
00:27:49,540 --> 00:27:55,400
See, prestige, influence, power, and wealth, none of these will water your soul like Jesus.

251
00:27:57,700 --> 00:28:03,580
See, Jesus' Sermon on the Mount wasn't a recruiting call for the strongest among you, or the smartest, or the most influential.

252
00:28:03,580 --> 00:28:08,500
It was a recruiting call for the heart, for a heart willing to be molded.

253
00:28:08,500 --> 00:28:10,780
Here's the hard truth.

254
00:28:10,780 --> 00:28:13,560
That makes people laugh.

255
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:21,320
Let me just take a pause here and say we're not going, like, maybe Ryan set it up that we're going to one sermon after I preach.

